{
  "rationale": "Iteration 0 has no race data or evaluator feedback, so this is a conservative baseline built from the contract. Geometry: five line sensors spread evenly across the body at x = -0.02, -0.01, 0, 0.01, 0.02 m, all 0.05 m ahead of the axle. Sensing ahead of the axle lets the controller react before the wheels reach a bend. The 12 mm footprint is about half the 25 mm tape width, so the sensors respond smoothly as the line moves under them. The 0.12 m wheel track and 0.03 m wheel radius give moderate turning authority, and the 0.8 kg mass with a 0.12 m body width keeps the yaw inertia modest. The body width of 0.12 m sets the off-track limit at max(0.06, 0.0125 + 0.03) = 0.06 m, which is the tighter bound, so a wider body would add little. Controller: sensor weights are proportional to lateral position (-2, -1, 0, 1, 2). Positive signal means left, so a line on the left gives a positive signal and steers left, which is correct. kp = 1.5 gives a turn of about 3 at full-scale error, which is enough to recover without saturating. kd = 0.05 damps the oscillation that a high kp would otherwise cause. ki = 0.1 is small so the integral does not wind up on long bends. base_speed = 1.6 (about 80 percent of full PWM) is chosen to finish under 3 s (about 1.5 m/s average) while leaving room to slow for sharp bends. line_loss = last_direction, so the robot turns back toward the side it last saw the line. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with rms_error around 0.02 to 0.04 m. The slalom may show more error where the bends are sharper. Hypotheses to test: (1) base_speed of 1.6 is too fast for the slalom and causes line loss there; (2) kp of 1.5 is low enough that rms_error stays high on the s-bend. Measurements requested below will show whether completion time meets the 3 s budget and where line loss occurs.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.01, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.01, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.18,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.6,
    "kp": 1.5,
    "ki": 0.1,
    "kd": 0.05,
    "sensor_weights": [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation",
      "control_effort"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor robot",
      "notes": "First candidate, built from the contract without race data: five evenly spaced sensors, proportional weights, kp 1.5, kd 0.05, base speed 1.6. It is a conservative baseline to measure against, not a tuned design."
    }
  }
}
